Once a base color is chosen, an interface needs more than five swatches. It needs tints and shades for backgrounds, borders, hover states and text. UI Colors takes a single value and generates that full range, from the lightest step to the darkest.

Used together, the first gives you the idea and the second makes it usable in a real product.', array['coolors', 'ui-colors']::text[], '2026-10-12T00:00:00.000Z'),
  ('study-ui-motion', 'Where to study good UI motion', 'Three references for animation that feels intentional instead of decorative.', 'Motion', 'Good motion is mostly invisible: it explains where something came from and confirms that an action worked. The fastest way to learn it is to study real examples.

60fps collects interactions recorded from shipping apps, sorted by pattern. Design Spells focuses on the small, delightful details that make a product feel considered. Easing is a reference of easing curves, so you can see how an animation accelerates and settles before you write a line of CSS.', array['60fps', 'design-spells', 'easing']::text[], '2026-10-11T23:59:00.000Z'),
  ('free-browser-design-stack', 'A free design stack that runs in the browser', 'Photopea, Fontshare and Phosphor cover image editing, type and icons — no installs, no licenses.', 'Assets', 'You can do a surprising amount of design work without installing anything. Photopea runs a Photoshop-style editor in the browser and opens PSD files.

For type, Fontshare offers free, high-quality fonts from the Indian Type Foundry. For icons, Phosphor is a flexible family you can tune in weight and size to match your interface.', array['photopea', 'fontshare', 'phosphor-icons']::text[], '2026-10-11T23:58:00.000Z');

